{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn","id":35860,"title":"Champions, Immortals, and Godborn","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-23T15:48:04-08:00","id":35860,"title":"Champions, Immortals, and Godborn","content":"Something I\u2019d like to see support for in Scion 2e is playing characters who <i>aren\u2019t</i> Scions. As I envision them, there would be three kinds of non-Scion protagonists:<ul><li><i>Champions</i> start out as (extra)ordinary mortals and have the potential to ascend to a Hero-like status despite their lack of any known divine heritage. They can\u2019t go beyond the Hero tier on their own though. The purpose of Champions is to allow for heroes of legend and mythology who <i>don\u2019t</i> have any known divine heritage.</li> <li>\u201c<i>Immortal</i>\u201d is a catchall term for semihuman or inhuman beings such as those described in 1e\u2019s <b>Scion: Hero</b> and <b>Scion: Demigod</b>. They exist on par with Heroes and Demigods, and those who start out Hero-like have the potential to ascend to a Demigod-like status; but they cannot achieve Godlike status without help.</li> <li>The <i>Godborn</i> are like Scions, except that both of their parents are gods and they start as Demigods or Gods in their own right. They exist because most gods in mythology don\u2019t fit the \u201cScion\u201d model. Their stories ought to revolve around learning about the World from an outsider\u2019s perspective.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Scions would still be the default protagonists of the game, and the only characters who inherently have the full upward mobility to transition all the way from Origins to God. Champions and even Immortals ought to be \u201cadoptable\u201d, a process by which a God takes a particularly worthy Champion or Immortal and makes him just like a Scion (giving \u201cvirgin gods\u201d like Artemis another option besides adopting another God\u2019s Scions or violating her virgin status if she wants Scions of her own). Such a process should be easier for Champions than for Immortals, and should still take more work than just procreating. <br /> <br /> Conversely, there might be an option by which a Godborn\u2019s parents can strip him of his power, reducing him to Hero or even Origin status: this is something of a postmodern concept, but is useful in that it allows he Godborn to participate in Origin- or Hero-level games. <br /> <br /> But for the most part, Champions, Immortals, and Godborn aren\u2019t intended for games that transition more than one stage. A game about Champions may transition from Origins to Hero at some point; but if/when it does, that will be near the culmination of the Champion's story \u2014 whereas for a Scion, transitioning from Origins to Hero is pretty much where the story begins. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T15:55:50-08:00","id":35868,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Champions myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T16:33:08-08:00","id":35904,"title":"","content":"With certain conditions, I don't have a problem with that. It's perfectly valid to run games that don't extend from Hero to God. It can be totally cool to run a Hero-only game, or a Hero+Demigod only game. God is really its own entire game by itself. Everything changes when you cross from Legend 8 to Legend 9.<br /> <br /> The first condition would be no adoptions. A Scion is part human, part God. That's the definition of a Scion. A dwarf can't become a Scion of Odin, ever. They can become an amazingly powerful dwarf, but they're always a dwarf because that's their Legend. The second condition would be this coming in <i>waaaay</i> down the line. Get Scion right first. Then do crazy stuff, if you must.<br /> <br /> I like Scion being a game about playing the children of Gods. That's what it said it was on the box, that's what I'd like to have inside the box when I open it. It didn't say &quot;modern epic fantasy&quot; or &quot;urban fantasy kitchen sink&quot;, it said &quot;children of the Gods&quot;. Cool, sold. And I think it loses something of its specialness when you turn Scion into urban-fantasy-kitchen-sink with angels, demons, dwarves, elves, saints, naga and Superman as playable characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T17:05:10-08:00","id":35926,"title":"","content":"Champions sounds like the intent behind Origin, which will probably cover the rules for deities to adopt people without any recent divine lineage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T18:03:09-08:00","id":35966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=35904#post35904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With certain conditions, I don't have a problem with that. It's perfectly valid to run games that don't extend from Hero to God. It can be totally cool to run a Hero-only game, or a Hero+Demigod only game. God is really its own entire game by itself. Everything changes when you cross from Legend 8 to Legend 9.</div> </div> </div> </div>There have been hints that in 2e, the transition from Hero to Demigod is going to be more pronounced than it was in 1e. Exactly how they differ is currently unknown; but it may be such that Hero -&gt; Demigod is comparable to Demigod -&gt; God. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=35904#post35904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first condition would be no adoptions. A Scion is part human, part God. That's the definition of a Scion. A dwarf can't become a Scion of Odin, ever. They can become an amazingly powerful dwarf, but they're always a dwarf because that's their Legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps. I don\u2019t think an adoption system would be entirely out of place, as long as there are sufficient hurdles to prevent it from eroding the specialness of Scions too much. And I\u2019m fine with it being presented as an optional system, so people like you can dismiss it with minimal hassle. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=35904#post35904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The second condition would be this coming in <i>waaaay</i> down the line. Get Scion right first. Then do crazy stuff, if you must.<br /> <br /> I like Scion being a game about playing the children of Gods. That's what it said it was on the box, that's what I'd like to have inside the box when I open it. It didn't say &quot;modern epic fantasy&quot; or &quot;urban fantasy kitchen sink&quot;, it said &quot;children of the Gods&quot;. Cool, sold. And I think it loses something of its specialness when you turn Scion into urban-fantasy-kitchen-sink with angels, demons, dwarves, elves, saints, naga and Superman as playable characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>The slippery slope argument: if we give an inch, they\u2019ll take a mile. There\u2019s a middle ground between \u201cchildren of the gods of myth\u201d and \u201curban fantasy kitchen sink\u201d. As you\u2019ve probablt noticed elsewhere, my own preference is to keep the focus on real-world mythology returning to the modern world, with the children of the gods at the vanguard of said return but not holding a monopoly on it. <br /> <br /> Personally, I\u2019d want Champions, Immortals, and Godborn in <b>Origins</b>, <b>Hero</b>, and <b>Demigod</b>, respectively; failing that, I\u2019d want them featured in the 2e\u2019s counterpart to <b>Scion Companion</b>, a fifth book in the series. It\u2019s not something to be postponed for an arbitrarily distant \u201cdown the road\u201d, like inclusions of Santa Claus or Superman would be; rather, it\u2019s an essential part of the toolkit for enabling as much of real-world mythology as possible. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T18:15:59-08:00","id":35970,"title":"","content":"There <i>is</i> a middle ground, but that middle ground is no longer &quot;children of the gods&quot;. It's already moved past that. By virtue of moving past that, I'm already unhappy. I don't think Scion <i>needs</i> to be a game that covers <i>all of mythology</i> as <i>playable characters</i>. It can include elves, dwarves, nymphs, etc., but it doesn't need them to be playable. VtM doesn't set out to be a game that includes all forms of playable supernatural creatures, it's about playing <i>vampires</i>. The worst bloodlines, the ones that are the poorest written and least effective in games, are the ones like Kiasyd (elves), Lhiannan (dryads) and Gargoyles (gargoyles), that try to bring <i>non-vampire things</i> into the game by making them somehow be vampires.<br /> <br /> Now, one thing that Scion2 promises is alternate settings. That's cool. There can be all kinds of alternate takes on Scion, <i>including</i> one where it <i>is</i> about all kinds of mythic creatures running around, being player characters. It can be Scion: Modern Mythos or Scion: Immortals. That's fine. But such alternate takes don't need to be incorporated into the <i>base setting</i> because that base setting needs to focus on getting Scions right and setting up a strong base to expand from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T18:43:11-08:00","id":35994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=35970#post35970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There <i>is</i> a middle ground, but that middle ground is no longer &quot;children of the gods&quot;. It's already moved past that. By virtue of moving past that, I'm already unhappy. I don't think Scion <i>needs</i> to be a game that covers <i>all of mythology</i> as <i>playable characters</i>. It can include elves, dwarves, nymphs, etc., but it doesn't need them to be playable. VtM doesn't set out to be a game that includes all forms of playable supernatural creatures, it's about playing <i>vampires</i>. The worst bloodlines, the ones that are the poorest written and least effective in games, are the ones like Kiasyd (elves), Lhiannan (dryads) and Gargoyles (gargoyles), that try to bring <i>non-vampire things</i> into the game by making them somehow be vampires.<br /> <br /> Now, one thing that Scion2 promises is alternate settings. That's cool. There can be all kinds of alternate takes on Scion, <i>including</i> one where it <i>is</i> about all kinds of mythic creatures running around, being player characters. It can be Scion: Modern Mythos or Scion: Immortals. That's fine. But such alternate takes don't need to be incorporated into the <i>base setting</i> because that base setting needs to focus on getting Scions right and setting up a strong base to expand from.</div> </div> </div> </div>VTM isn't a comparable line. A comparable line would be Exalted or as a whole The World of darkness (New or old whichever) Scion isn't just a single part of a whole but an entire universe. Whether this means non-demigods should be playable or not isn't my point but I don't think you are making an apt comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T18:43:19-08:00","id":35996,"title":"","content":"<b>Vampire</b> <i>does</i> include support for playing ghouls and hunters as well as vampires; but it\u2019s also worth noting that <b>Vampire</b> is one of nine or ten gamelines set in a common setting, whereas <b>Scion</b> is more like <b>Exalted</b> in than it encapsulates the entire setting: what <b>Scion</b> doesn\u2019t permit isn\u2019t permitted anywhere in the setting. <b>Exalted</b> is primarily about the Solar Exalted; but it provides options for plenty of other playable character types. Nobody forces you to use any of them, mind you; but they\u2019re there just the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T19:04:57-08:00","id":36005,"title":"","content":"Exalted is about the Exalted, not just Solars. Its original premise was being the Chosen of the Gods. It did, much, much later, allow for non-Exalted PCs, but that was.. much, much later. It wasn't until very late in First Edition that Exalted expanded to allow non-Exalted PCs. We're talking like last two or three books released for the setting included rules for being X-blooded, Fae, Dragon-Kings, etc. It was possible straight out of the box to be a Heroic Mortal, but then again in Scion it's possible to play a mortal character, too. They just aren't an intended type of PC and don't get material devoted to them. They're incidentally playable since rules for them happen to exist as a by-product of the setting.<br /> <br /> While New World of Darkness is a cohesive, single setting, Old World of Darkness is not. Each gameline was by itself, by default. Trying to reconcile Demon: the Fallen and Werewolf: the Apocalypse is a recipe for any number of agonizing headaches. I'm pretty comfortable with my comparison. The Old World of Darkness kind of split is exactly what I'd be fine with in Scion, if you must offer support for non-Scions. Alternate settings that don't have to interact unless the Storyteller of your game wants to bring them together. Write Scion, the core game line, and then later write Scion: Immortals as an alternate take on the setting that can be used on its own, or in collaboration with Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T20:25:32-08:00","id":36052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36005#post36005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted is about the Exalted, not just Solars. Its original premise was being the Chosen of the Gods. It did, much, much later, allow for non-Exalted PCs, but that was.. much, much later. It wasn't until very late in First Edition that Exalted expanded to allow non-Exalted PCs. We're talking like last two or three books released for the setting included rules for being X-blooded, Fae, Dragon-Kings, etc. It was possible straight out of the box to be a Heroic Mortal, but then again in Scion it's possible to play a mortal character, too. They just aren't an intended type of PC and don't get material devoted to them. They're incidentally playable since rules for them happen to exist as a by-product of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. But we\u2019re not talking 1e Scion here; we\u2019re talking 2e Scion, which is arguably more comparable to 3e Exalted, or at least 2e Exalted. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36005#post36005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While New World of Darkness is a cohesive, single setting, Old World of Darkness is not. Each gameline was by itself, by default. Trying to reconcile Demon: the Fallen and Werewolf: the Apocalypse is a recipe for any number of agonizing headaches. I'm pretty comfortable with my comparison. The Old World of Darkness kind of split is exactly what I'd be fine with in Scion, if you must offer support for non-Scions. Alternate settings that don't have to interact unless the Storyteller of your game wants to bring them together. Write Scion, the core game line, and then later write Scion: Immortals as an alternate take on the setting that can be used on its own, or in collaboration with Scion.</div> </div> </div> </div>First, it appears that we\u2019re on the same page about at least one thing: nobody should be forced to include playable Immortals in their <b>Scion</b> game if they don\u2019t want to. I haven\u2019t suggested such a thing, and I don\u2019t think that anyone has done so \u2014 because it would be a stupid thing to attempt. With that said: \u200b<br /> <br /> oWoD\u2019s lack of cohesiveness was a major source of complaints from the fans, which is why nWoD has much more cohesiveness to it. The model of making it so that you\u2019ll have headaches if you try to mix Werewolf and Demon doesn\u2019t strike me as being the sort of thing that ought to be emulated. But even looking at the nWoD: Werewolf and Demon are different gamelines because they have virtually no setting overlap (Werewolf doesn\u2019t include angels or Stigmatics; Demon doesn\u2019t include spirits or shapeshifters) with wildly different themes (spirituality and savage fury vs. techgnostic espionage).<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t see Champions, Immortals, and Godborn being <i>that</i> different from Scions: they share the common theme of authentic mythology resurgent in the modern world, and are more akin to <b>Vampire</b>\u2019s ghouls and hunters (if you <i>must</i> use a WoD analogy) or to <b>Exalted</b>\u2019s God-Blooded and Fair Folk: they\u2019re integral to the setting even when you <i>don\u2019t</i> make them available as playable characters. <br /> <br /> Now, something like a game that features the likes of Pecos Bill and Santa Claus? <i>that</i> would be analogous to <b>Werewolf</b> vs. <b>Demon</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T20:44:12-08:00","id":36062,"title":"","content":"Exalted is a giant mess of awful in its quest to be the big tent for all fantasy role-players to get their DBZ on under. I would rather not see something like that happen to Scion.<br /> <br /> The diluting of the core product is certainly not WW/OPP's sin alone, but they are perhaps the worst repeat offenders in the industry. Storyteller/Storytelling/Storyfap or whatever it is being called these days isn't presented as a system toolkit intended to support a wide array of games, it's presented as a group of mechanically-related but distinct games. Trying to fit more themes into a single setting inevitably causes thematic drift that hurts the overall tone of the game. (&quot;Forever unclean!&quot;)<br /> <br /> With that said, I don't object to any of Dataweaver's proposals as possible ground for exploration. I don't think they should necessarily be included in the core rules with the possible exception of Champions, which seems like the sort of thing that's been missing from the game's core systems. I think the game loses nothing exploring the more complicated sections of mythology, like ascended monkeys and fully divine children as playable characters. I also think that only a narrow handful of games and gamers would actually benefit from specific rules for handling those kinds of characters, however. You could probably cover the latter two concepts easily in sidebars, honestly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T20:45:53-08:00","id":36063,"title":"","content":"They are integral to the setting, but <i>not</i> as PCs. That can come later. They don't need equal attention to Scions. The game is about Scions, and it should always be about Scions. If there is demand, later, once Scions are set up and polished, then add other stuff. The same way Exalted did, the same way Vampire did. Rules for playable Ghouls and Hunters weren't released until years into VtM, same with Exalted.<br /> <br /> I also happen to <i>loathe</i> Exalted 2nd Edition because I feel it entirely abandoned the original flavor of Exalted in favor of anime and generic &quot;fantasy&quot; tropes. It went from &quot;Epic&quot; to &quot;L33+&quot; and I was sad. So sad that I never bought a single Ex2 book. Ex3 may surprise me, I hope it does, but it's also making big changes to the original core of Exalted and many of them I do not like. It's not cool that there are Exalted of Little Gods. That's what Godblooded were for. Exalted should be special. But, I'm reserving judgement (kinda) until the final product comes out and I see how long it takes them to deal with all the fiddly little silly stuff they seem to want to add. I would hope that they get the Big Five set up and polished before bothering with playable Blooded, Fae, Spirits, Minor Exalted and suchnot. <br /> <br /> The lack of cohesiveness in WoD allowed for each splat to be totally faithful to its <i>own themes</i>. Werewolf didn't have to compromise itself to include Demon material, and vice versa. That's what I want. If you want Scion: Scions, you don't have to take Scion: Everything and try to dig out the parts you don't like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T21:38:25-08:00","id":36100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36062#post36062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted is a giant mess of awful in its quest to be the big tent for all fantasy role-players to get their DBZ on under. I would rather not see something like that happen to Scion.<br /> <br /> The diluting of the core product is certainly not WW/OPP's sin alone, but they are perhaps the worst repeat offenders in the industry. Storyteller/Storytelling/Storyfap or whatever it is being called these days isn't presented as a system toolkit intended to support a wide array of games, it's presented as a group of mechanically-related but distinct games. Trying to fit more themes into a single setting inevitably causes thematic drift that hurts the overall tone of the game. (&quot;Forever unclean!&quot;)<br /> <br /> With that said, I don't object to any of Dataweaver's proposals as possible ground for exploration. I don't think they should necessarily be included in the core rules with the possible exception of Champions, which seems like the sort of thing that's been missing from the game's core systems. I think the game loses nothing exploring the more complicated sections of mythology, like ascended monkeys and fully divine children as playable characters. I also think that only a narrow handful of games and gamers would actually benefit from specific rules for handling those kinds of characters, however. You could probably cover the latter two concepts easily in sidebars, honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. In fact, I don\u2019t think <i>any</i> of the three would need more than a sidebar: a paragraph or so to explain the concept, and a few more to outline the needed tweaks. I\u2019m not suggesting that they get equal time with Scions, or that the focus of the game be diverted from Scions; but you don\u2019t have to postpone everything that isn\u2019t Scions to keep them as the central focus of the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36063#post36063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lack of cohesiveness in WoD allowed for each splat to be totally faithful to its <i>own themes</i>. Werewolf didn't have to compromise itself to include Demon material, and vice versa. That's what I want. If you want Scion: Scions, you don't have to take Scion: Everything and try to dig out the parts you don't like.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said before, I\u2019m not arguing for an urban fantasy kitchen sink.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-24-2013, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T21:53:03-08:00","id":36112,"title":"","content":"I don't think adding playable Dwarves is so simple it could be explained in a sidebar. They'd need rules for progression, how their powers work, caps on their abilities, their entire racial power of wonder-forging actually explained and systemized... if you want them as <i>actual playable characters, </i>they need their own set of rules. That's gunna be more than a page or two. I have no objection to Scion: Immortals being a big-book that gets published later on, but all they need in the corebooks is the same treatment they got in Hero.<br /> <br /> Technically, you can use the Exalted Corebook to 'play' a Sidereal. They explain how the dice-adders work and generally describe the theme of their charms. Nothing stops you from just reskinning Solar Charms and calling the resulting creature a Sidereal. Same for Scion. Nothing <i>stops</i> you from playing a Dwarf given the template in the Antagonist/NPC chapter. They just aren't fully developed. If you want them fully developed, much less <i>all the Lesser Immortals, Legendary Mortals and NewBorn Gods ever</i>, then you need a whole book for that. Maybe multiple mini-books. It's not a sidebar type of thing. If you're gunna do something, do it right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T22:31:27-08:00","id":36150,"title":"","content":"You have a point about the Immortals \u2014 although it\u2019s a testament to the versatility of <b>Scion</b> that its Boons probably <i>could</i> cover the powers of the Immortals without needing to craft whole new systems for them. You need rules for dwarves forging magical artifacts? Use the same ones that Hephaestus uses when <i>he</i> forges magical artifacts, or a subset of the same. Contrast this with Exalted, where Solar Charms don\u2019t really cover the ground that Sidereal Charms need to cover. <br /> <br /> But I don\u2019t see why Champions or Godborn would need special power sets of their own. Champions would use a subset of the same mechanics that Heroes do, and the Godborn would use the same rules as Demigods and Gods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T22:38:03-08:00","id":36155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36150#post36150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have a point about the Immortals \u2014 although it\u2019s a testament to the versatility of <b>Scion</b> that its Boons probably <i>could</i> cover the powers of the Immortals without needing to craft whole new systems for them. You need rules for dwarves forging magical artifacts? Use the same ones that Hephaestus uses when <i>he</i> forges magical artifacts, or a subset of the same. Contrast this with Exalted, where Solar Charms don\u2019t really cover the ground that Sidereal Charms need to cover.<br /> <br /> But I don\u2019t see why Champions or Godborn would need special power sets of their own. Champions would use a subset of the same mechanics that Heroes do, and the Godborn would use the same rules as Demigods and Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going to tentatively concur with you. But it's going to depend on how Scion 2 sets up power progression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T22:44:54-08:00","id":36161,"title":"","content":"True enough. I know what I\u2019d prefer (I outlined it on the Linear vs. Cloud thread); but there\u2019s no guarantee we\u2019ll get it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T22:52:33-08:00","id":36166,"title":"","content":"Godborn, yes, but Legendary Mortals don't need or deserve access to the same powers Scions have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T23:04:17-08:00","id":36174,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s a reason I\u2019ve been saying \u201cChampions\u201d and not \u201cLegendary Mortals\u201d. I <i>do</i> think that advanced Champions ought to be able to hold their own with Heroes, including Legend 4, Epic Attributes, Knacks, and the same sort of Boons that Heroes have. The main catch is that that describes the upper limit of a Champion\u2019s power; a Hero can still advance to Demigod and then God. But even if we were to go with Legendary Mortals a la Scion 1e, I don\u2019t see why they\u2019d need their own powers: a (very limited) subset of the powers available to Heroes should suffice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T23:25:09-08:00","id":36189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36174#post36174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s a reason I\u2019ve been saying \u201cChampions\u201d and not \u201cLegendary Mortals\u201d. I <i>do</i> think that advanced Champions ought to be able to hold their own with Heroes, including Legend 4, Epic Attributes, Knacks, and the same sort of Boons that Heroes have. The main catch is that that describes the upper limit of a Champion\u2019s power; a Hero can still advance to Demigod and then God. But even if we were to go with Legendary Mortals a la Scion 1e, I don\u2019t see why they\u2019d need their own powers: a (very limited) subset of the powers available to Heroes should suffice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strongly agree with your opinion and the conclusions that follow it with regards to this. No offense, Telgar, but providing a sidebar for legendary mortals++ doesn't hurt the game in any way I can conceive of. Especially if there are also rules for gods to adopt them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T00:39:03-08:00","id":36217,"title":"","content":"It makes Scions less special. Why would the Gods return to the World, go through the hassle of fathering/bearing Scions if they can just adopt mortals, or bang other Gods/magical critters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T01:00:25-08:00","id":36224,"title":"","content":"Champions, I like. Having a system in place to model heroes like Jason or Odysseus would not be amiss in a game of this nature. Immortals I'm a bit on the fence about. I do not think I would ever use them, but I do not see the harm in having a separate supplement regarding playing them that I can happily ignore.<br /> <br /> Godborn though, I definitely do not like. If Gods can so readily create new Gods, then why are they creating Scions? At the end of the day, Scions are soldiers, created to fight in the Titanomachy. If the Gods can create soldiers along their general level of power then they would have zero need to go to the hassle of fathering/bearing Scions and <i>then</i> waiting for them to grow up and <i>then</i> Visiting them and <i>then</i> waiting for those Scions to grow to Godhood <i>before</i> drafting them into the main Titan War in the Overworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T01:09:35-08:00","id":36228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36217#post36217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes Scions less special. Why would the Gods return to the World, go through the hassle of fathering/bearing Scions if they can just adopt mortals, or bang other Gods/magical critters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Scions tend to be agents of major cultural change in the world, kings and queens, legendary heroes, so forth, which is a large part of building an army to fight the Titans.<br /> <br /> Because they are humans moving in the human world, they can effect cultural change within that world much more easily. When they begin to accumulate power and become demigods and eventually mantle the responsibilities of godhood, they're still carrying recent experience with humanity that their divine forbears don't have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T01:11:28-08:00","id":36229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36217#post36217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes Scions less special. Why would the Gods return to the World, go through the hassle of fathering/bearing Scions if they can just adopt mortals, or bang other Gods/magical critters?</div> </div> </div> </div> I know you intended that to be a rhetorical question; but let\u2019s take it seriously:<br /> <br /> 1. Implicit in your question is the notion that just anyone could be adopted under the system I\u2019m suggesting. That\u2019s where the \u201cright stuff\u201d part of my proposal comes in: not just anyone can be a Champion; and only Champions can be adopted. What is this \u201cright stuff\u201d I\u2019m talking about? Unknown, and a deliberate mystery \u2014 perhaps they\u2019re chosen by Fate. Ultimately, a mortal has the right stuff to become a Champion if the Storyteller says he does; and there\u2019s no known way to predict who has it and who doesn\u2019t. Why procreate with humans instead of adopting them? Because you <i>know</i> that your scion can become a Hero, Demigod, and eventually God. You generally don\u2019t know that someone is a Champion until he\u2019s already attained Hero-like status; and it generally doesn\u2019t happen often. Which means that when they <i>do</i> appear, there\u2019s often a lot of competition over them.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s also possible that adopting a human takes something out of you \u2014 say, a permanent dot of Willpower or even Legend: something that you can recover given some time, so it\u2019s not like you permanently weaken yourself by \u201cadopting\u201d; but it would mean that adoptions don\u2019t happen on a whim.<br /> <br /> 2. Gods <i>can</i> bang other gods; that\u2019s where most Gods come from, after all. So let me ask you: why <i>would</i> they return to the World and procreate with humans when they can procreate without ever leaving the Overworld? Especially considering that the Godborn start out <i>at least</i> as Demigods, and most commonly as full-fledged Gods. Sure, they can\u2019t transition all the way from mortal to god; but that\u2019s because they skip the first two or three stages. What do Scions get that makes them more worthwhile than the Godborn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-24-2013, 07:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T01:28:15-08:00","id":36235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36228#post36228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scions tend to be agents of major cultural change in the world, kings and queens, legendary heroes, so forth, which is a large part of building an army to fight the Titans.<br /> <br /> Because they are humans moving in the human world, they can effect cultural change within that world much more easily. When they begin to accumulate power and become demigods and eventually mantle the responsibilities of godhood, they're still carrying recent experience with humanity that their divine forbears don't have.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of which is particularly helpful in fighting the Titans. Titans don't care if the majority of humanity hates them. They're Titans. Gaia could destroy entire cities with little effort, and the combined forces of all the Titans would crush Humanity like a bug. Similarly, the Gods don't gain any actual power from worship (except the Aztecs) so converting mortal nations and affecting cultural change, while a very nice gesture for Mother's Day, and a great victory for any PC, isn't actually something the Gods have the time to be excited about.<br /> <br /> There's a reason the Gods are fielding Scions again after so many ages, and that reason isn't 'make the mortals love us again', it's WAR. And the introduction of the Godborn as player options is effectively rendering the entire 'main' splat redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T01:32:27-08:00","id":36237,"title":"","content":"1) Yes, but they're still out there and competing for the same jobs as Scions. They have their own niche. Enkidu doesn't need to be as awesome as Gilgamesh. That's not his narrative role. Iolaus isn't as awesome as Hercules. I don't mind Legendary Mortals, but they don't need to just Scions that don't have a godly parent. If they're going to exist, they need to be their own thing.<br /> <br /> 2) Creating a new God carries a <i>lot</i> of baggage. Most Heroes don't become Demigods and most Demigods don't become Gods. It's a small chance that your new offspring is going to decide to ascend to Godhood and start horning in on your territory, taking your stuff and generally getting in your way. Look at Hermes. Day 1, starts bothering Apollo. Scions are going to take a long time to reach apotheosis, if they ever do. They're also going to have a mortal mindset and mortal upbringing, something that Gods never, ever have. They think differently, they bring different advantages. And they're far less prone to Fatebonding while they're Demigods and Heroes.<br /> <br /> Scions are a pretty perfect deal. They have the <i>potential</i> to become heavy hitters in the War, but they don't just start off ruining your day with their antics. You have time to prep for it, and while they're mortal, you can do a lot of things to them you couldn't get away with doing to a God.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T03:16:01-08:00","id":36275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36237#post36237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Yes, but they're still out there and competing for the same jobs as Scions. They have their own niche. Enkidu doesn't need to be as awesome as Gilgamesh. That's not his narrative role. Iolaus isn't as awesome as Hercules. I don't mind Legendary Mortals, but they don't need to just Scions that don't have a godly parent. If they're going to exist, they need to be their own thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not talking about Scions and their sidekicks; I\u2019m talking about Arthur and Merlin, or Jason and the Argonauts (at least three of whom were Scions). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36237#post36237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Creating a new God carries a <i>lot</i> of baggage. Most Heroes don't become Demigods and most Demigods don't become Gods. It's a small chance that your new offspring is going to decide to ascend to Godhood and start horning in on your territory, taking your stuff and generally getting in your way. Look at Hermes. Day 1, starts bothering Apollo. Scions are going to take a long time to reach apotheosis, if they ever do. They're also going to have a mortal mindset and mortal upbringing, something that Gods never, ever have. They think differently, they bring different advantages. And they're far less prone to Fatebonding while they're Demigods and Heroes.<br /> <br /> Scions are a pretty perfect deal. They have the <i>potential</i> to become heavy hitters in the War, but they don't just start off ruining your day with their antics. You have time to prep for it, and while they're mortal, you can do a lot of things to them you couldn't get away with doing to a God.</div> </div> </div> </div>Samudra: does this answer your concerns about Godborn? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T03:27:35-08:00","id":36277,"title":"","content":"I do like your ideas, Dataweaver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T03:36:46-08:00","id":36281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36275#post36275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Samudra: does this answer your concerns about Godborn?</div> </div> </div> </div>To a large extent, yes. I suppose Scions, after apotheosis, would be easier to direct into battle once they've spent a mortal lifetime fighting the Titans minions. Nevertheless, I doubt any of them will get much time to 'learn about the World from an outsider's perspective'. Beings of their power level are too precious to waste on the World unless one of the Titan's own champions, such as Sinmore, comes down first.<br /> <br /> That being said, I still hate them as player characters. Only I can happily admit now that my problems with them are entirely personal and I will simply be ignoring them if they make it into 2e so eberybody's happy.<br /> <br /> I am fond of the other two splats though <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T04:50:24-08:00","id":36298,"title":"","content":"I like the idea as a general rule of thumb. How do you classify mortals with no (apparent) divine heritage who are elevated to divinity? Or mortals who do incredible or terrible things to make themselves part divine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T05:25:24-08:00","id":36311,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d classify them both as Champions who get \u201cadopted\u201d: in the former case, the Champion gets the attention of a God who decides that he\u2019s worthy of Godhood and adopts him; in the latter case, the \u201cadopter\u201d is either forced into it (you <i>did</i> say \u201cdo incredible or terrible things\u201d; and compelling a god to empower you certainly qualifies) or is a particularly unsavory type who considers the terrible things the \u201cChampion\u201d has done are grounds for promoting him. <br /> <br /> In <b>Scion</b>, nobody is ever elevated to divinity overnight; myths along those lines need to be modified to include a period of time that the candidate for apotheosis spent rising through the ranks of power. As well, as I see it, nobody is ever spontaneously elevated to divinity: the elevation is always sponsored by a divine being (either a God or a Titan). Scions get Visitations that transition them from mortal to Hero; Champions need to get Adopted before they can transition from Hero to Demigod. <br /> <br /> And thanks for the \u201cno (apparent) divine heritage\u201d line. As I said, as I see it, what makes one a Champion is a mystery: one possible answer to it is that divine heritage might be \u201cgenetic\u201d, for lack of a better term: that is, it gets passed down from parent to child. But if so, the way that it does so should be obscure and unpredictable: e.g., most immediate children of a Scion <i>aren\u2019t</i>, and the status usually skips multiple generations. It may well be that it this point, the Mitochondrial Eve or one of her ancestors might have been a (very early) Scion, in which case Champion status could potentially manifest in <i>anyone</i>. Or, as I said before, it might have nothing to do with the Gods, and Champions might be chosen by Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T05:53:47-08:00","id":36316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36311#post36311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...in the latter case, the \u201cadopter\u201d is either forced into it (you <i>did</i> say \u201cdo incredible or terrible things\u201d; and compelling a god to empower you certainly qualifies) or is a particularly unsavory type who considers the terrible things the \u201cChampion\u201d has done are grounds for promoting him.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> And thanks for the \u201cno (apparent) divine heritage\u201d line. As I said, as I see it, what makes one a Champion is a mystery: one possible answer to it is that divine heritage might be \u201cgenetic\u201d, for lack of a better term: that is, it gets passed down from parent to child. But if so, the way that it does so should be obscure and unpredictable: e.g., most immediate children of a Scion <i>aren\u2019t</i>, and the status usually skips multiple generations. It may well be that it this point, the Mitochondrial Eve or one of her ancestors might have been a (very early) Scion, in which case Champion status could potentially manifest in <i>anyone</i>. Or, as I said before, it might have nothing to do with the Gods, and Champions might be chosen by Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a very specific subset of Gods that are both antagonistic in nature and not quite fit for Titanhood, such as the Polynesian Whiro, who might sponsor an evil Champion.<br /> <br /> As for the last paragraph, I rather think a combination of both might be best. I like the idea that Champions are descended from a pre-apotheosis Scion somewhere up the line, but that Fate itself decides which one is so blessed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T06:08:11-08:00","id":36325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36316#post36316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the last paragraph, I rather think a combination of both might be best. I like the idea that Champions are descended from a pre-apotheosis Scion somewhere up the line, but that Fate itself decides which one is so blessed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also provides a fairly solid hook for a group who happens to have a Champion in their midst. &quot;So where did your mojo come from, anyhow?&quot; Easily a half dozen adventures spread out over the course of a campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T08:30:42-08:00","id":36390,"title":"","content":"Could someone explain to me the difference between Champions and what OPP is proposing for Origins? Because they seem like they're pretty similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T09:26:01-08:00","id":36418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36112#post36112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think adding playable Dwarves is so simple it could be explained in a sidebar.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Sometimes. Gods want to fuck dwarves. And animals. And occasionally trees. Once in a while a pile of dirt. Gods are kinky fuckers aren't they?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T09:39:14-08:00","id":36429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36418#post36418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Sometimes. Gods want to fuck dwarves. And animals. And occasionally trees. Once in a while a pile of dirt. Gods are kinky fuckers aren't they?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That explains where they come from. It does not come anywhere near making them playable. That would require rules for stat adjustments, inherent racial powers, a description of what powers they can learn, their place in the setting, native Terra Incognita etc. And then multiply that for Apsaras, Sidhe, Alfar, lesser Kami, Naga, Nymphs, Satyrs, Centaurs...etc.<br /> <br /> A sidebar will not cover it. Immortals needs to be it's own supplement, like Ghouls are for Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 12-24-2013, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T09:55:35-08:00","id":36435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36429#post36429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...then multiply that for Apsaras, Sidhe, Alfar, lesser Kami, Naga, Nymphs, Satyrs, Centaurs...etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's another issue with the idea. Creating a single system that represents <i>every single mythological creature, ever<b>. </b></i><b>Hot damn</b>, that is a crazy challenge. Scion's system only has to represent Scions, right now. Trying to invent one that models <i>everything ever</i> is a much bigger challenge because, no, just Purviews and Knacks isn't going to cover everything. You have things like Maenads being immune to fire <i>and metal</i>. Creatures like Dwarves that can magically forge artifacts with skill surpassing their Pantheon. The horrible, magical stench of Harpies. All kinds of unique racial powers that need to be quantified and balanced. It's a big mess trying to make <i>everything ever</i> a playable, fully developed race. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T10:47:55-08:00","id":36448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36435#post36435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's another issue with the idea. Creating a single system that represents <i>every single mythological creature, ever<b>. </b></i><b>Hot damn</b>, that is a crazy challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>is</i> a crazy challenge; though to be fair, I\u2019m not thinking in <i>quite</i> that expansive of terms. I\u2019m not quite sure where I\u2019d draw the line; I\u2019d probably insist on the Immortal being humanoid, for one thing: the system for Immortals wouldn\u2019t be designed with Unicorns, Pegasi, Manticores, or Dragons in mind. Still, this is the same company that\u2019s going to be publishing <b>Exalted 3e</b> with its Exigents, and the Trinity Continuum with its Novas. I do not doubt that they\u2019d be up to the challenge. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36435#post36435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scion's system only has to represent Scions, right now. Trying to invent one that models <i>everything ever</i> is a much bigger challenge because, no, just Purviews and Knacks isn't going to cover everything. You have things like Maenads being immune to fire <i>and metal</i>. Creatures like Dwarves that can magically forge artifacts with skill surpassing their Pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the former case, a lot of ground could be covered by breaking Boons out of Purviews where Immortals are concerned: immunity to fire and metal? Give the Maenads a Boon that grants immunity to fire and a Boon that grants immunity to metal; voila!<br /> <br /> In the latter case, I\u2019d contend that the Aesir rely on Dwarves who surpass them in the craftsmanship of the forge because they don\u2019t have a God of the Forge: a contest between the Nordic Dwarves and Hephaestus would be Epic. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ll grant that Boons, Epics, and Knacks can\u2019t cover <i>everything</i>; but I suspect that they can cover a hell of a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T11:02:54-08:00","id":36460,"title":"","content":"Or, it could possibly be done with a point based system. &quot;Immunity to ____ costs 4 points. So you need to buy a 4 point hindrance/flaw/condition/what-have-you to make up for that&quot;<br /> <br /> This would help out in customizing the various races and thus would not need to do the whole &quot;listing for everything&quot; issue that was brought up earlier by Telgar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T11:11:27-08:00","id":36466,"title":"","content":"Oh, horrors! Save us from point-based systems, that encourage people to think in terms of \u201cgame balance\u201d and turn them into point accountants who make character design decisions based on what\u2019s cost-effective rather than what fits the concept!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T11:13:15-08:00","id":36467,"title":"","content":"The problem with that is, it becomes all too easy to go away from mythology and start making up every random critter under the sun. It would serve the setting of the game to include Harpies and Gandharva, not Mothman. Besides, if you make it an optional point buy system, you end up with oddities like Harpies without a stench or Naga who can't breathe underwater because the player decided to spend all his points on refining flight or poison bites.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Basically what Dataweaver just said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T11:30:34-08:00","id":36475,"title":"","content":"Doing a bit of cross-thread posting: the recent discussion about Amazons in the Scion: Origins thread reminded me of my own thoughts about Wonder Woman. The current iteration of Wonder Woman (daughter of Hypollyta and Zeus) is a Scion. The previous version, aside from her Galatea-like \u201cbirth\u201d, was essentially a sort of Solar Exalt, but with the Greek Gods standing in for the Unconquered Sun. The original version of Wonder Woman, however, was a regular amazon who achieved superhuman feats through the wonders of \u201cAmazon Training\u201d \u2014 basically a Greek-flavored version of what we think of today as over-the-top martial arts movies such as <i>Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon</i>. That original version of Wonder Woman is what I tend to think of when I imagine Champions: neither born with divine blood nor granted powers by divine patrons, but instead attaining power through their own efforts and a quirk of Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T11:40:54-08:00","id":36480,"title":"","content":"Correct me if I am wrong, but was not even this original Wonder Woman a daughter of Hippolyta? In which case she has the blood of Ares in her. I know another origin story has her made out of clay, in which case she's not even quite human. Of course, that woman has had so many revamps I'm pretty sure I'm getting something mixed up somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T11:52:22-08:00","id":36486,"title":"","content":"She was at least one generation removed from Ares, if not entirely unrelated (the Galatea-like origin) \u2014 possibly making her an Immortal, depending on your view of what the Amazons should be like. But it\u2019s also worth noting that these early \u201cAmazon Training\u201d stories claimed that <i>any</i> woman could learn the techniques in question, not just Amazons, and demonstrated the fact on a few occasions. That\u2019s a recipe for gross abuse, of course, which is why I would give Champions some sort of \u201cright stuff\u201d ambiguous qualification that prevents it from being something that <i>everyone</i> can do while still leaving open the possibility that <i>anyone</i> might be a potential Champion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T12:08:37-08:00","id":36497,"title":"","content":"I prefer the idea of Champions as distantly related to the Gods, as you yourself suggested some posts ago, so any version of Wonder Woman that is actually born of Hippolyta would count. The Galatea Origin, however, especially followed by the power investiture by the Gods strikes me as a one off case of the Gods using a series of Avatars to create and empower a unique individual, which is such a niche concept (not to mention it just screams Mary Sue/Special Snowflake) that I don't think you could adequately model it in game mechanics, especially given that Avatars can do literally anything within that Purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T14:14:58-08:00","id":36555,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that when I suggested the \u201cdistantly related\u201d theory, I referenced the Mitochondrial Eve or one of her ancestors being a Scion \u2014 and thus <i>every human being living on the planet today</i> being \u201cdistantly related to the Gods\u201d. The whole point of the Champions is that it <i>isn\u2019t</i> any sort of unique heritage that empowers them, and <i>anyone</i> could turn out to be a Champion. There would probably be theories that Champions are more likely among the more immediate descendants of Scions; but there would be no evidence to support (or refute) such theories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T16:41:05-08:00","id":36624,"title":"","content":"See, I don't really like that just as a thesis. If you're getting all egalitarian and anyone can <i>earn</i> Legendary Status by just being awesome, then being <i>born</i> with your destiny seems a lot less special. It, in fact, makes Scions <i>less cool</i> than the guys that earned their awesome all by themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T18:45:46-08:00","id":36667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36624#post36624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I don't really like that just as a thesis. If you're getting all egalitarian and anyone can <i>earn</i> Legendary Status by just being awesome, then being <i>born</i> with your destiny seems a lot less special. It, in fact, makes Scions <i>less cool</i> than the guys that earned their awesome all by themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like post hoc justification; if we don't know where the Champions get their mojo, how do we know that they are anything different than Scions except they never got visitations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T19:03:34-08:00","id":36677,"title":"","content":"As well, it comes across as a particularly unsavory sort of elitism: \u201cwe must protect the special status of the privileged class from anything even hinting of a challenge to it, so we cannot allow anyone to be as awesome as even a Hero without having Better Blood.\u201d<br /> <br /> And again, you have the likes of Jason, who captained a crew consisting largely of Scions but was not himself a Scion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-24-2013, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T19:20:07-08:00","id":36685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36624#post36624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I don't really like that just as a thesis. If you're getting all egalitarian and anyone can <i>earn</i> Legendary Status by just being awesome, then being <i>born</i> with your destiny seems a lot less special. It, in fact, makes Scions <i>less cool</i> than the guys that earned their awesome all by themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention, those Champions, as per the original, could only reach Hero level things and not go to Demi-Godhood or above. So how can they be <i>more cool</i> than someone who can end up influencing nations and sinking continents?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T19:52:23-08:00","id":36697,"title":"","content":"To be fair, the original post qualified that with \u201c\u2026on his own\u201d: it allowed for \u201cadoption\u201d as a means for a Champion to gain all of the benefits of a Scion. OTOH, this is also why I suggested that such \u201cadoptions\u201d have a price to prevent them from being conducted too casually, and that they be presented as an option that the Storyteller needn\u2019t even permit. <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve gone out of my way at every turn to ensure that Champions don\u2019t supplant Scions as the stars of the show. Any more restrictions, and Champions cease to be interesting as a player character option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T19:58:49-08:00","id":36700,"title":"","content":"I read the original post to my Scion group and we all agreed that a supplement with these rules would be awesome to see and implement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T20:07:39-08:00","id":36705,"title":"","content":"Scion IS elitist. It's NOT based on the modern idea that hard work and effort can earn you a place in the stars. You have to be born to your destiny. That's kinda the point. You're Special from birth. You didn't bootstrap yourself to specialness and then convince a God you're so awesome that they should sacrifice some of their power to help you achieve even more. That's Exalted. It already exists. Scion is different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T20:36:06-08:00","id":36720,"title":"","content":"If you want to play it that way, it\u2019s no skin off my nose. My issue is when you insist that <i>everyone</i> should play it that way, that the game shouldn\u2019t support any other style of play than the one that you prefer. <br /> <br /> Yes, you\u2019ve made allowances for other rules down the road \u2014 but you\u2019ve done so grudgingly, with the implication that you\u2019d prefer that the can be kicked down the road indefinitely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T22:36:07-08:00","id":36780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=36705#post36705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scion IS elitist. It's NOT based on the modern idea that hard work and effort can earn you a place in the stars.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it's <i>not </i>a modern idea.<br /> It's an idea at least as old as the idea that one can only be <i>born </i>to greatness. It can be found in cultures all over the world and even in mythology that's found within the game itself.<br /> <br /> Heroism isn't in the circumstances of your birth. It's in the decisions and actions you make throughout your life. And no, that is not a modern idea either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 12-25-2013, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T06:26:49-08:00","id":36897,"title":"","content":"In Telgar's defence, Scion's mythological background lends itself to an elitist feel the way Vampire encourages a horror one. World Mythology makes it very clear that the Gods are on a level above humanity. Humanity might (rarely) reach divinity, but most of the time it's by accident or because an already existing God took an interest in them. Even non-Scion heroes like Jason and Odysseus only succeed through divine help.<br /> <br /> Now, if this were a game like Mage, then a human being (eventually) forcing Zeus to wash his car or Isis to do the dishes would be totally in line with the core concepts of the game, and would be awesome. But Scion has a different source, and thus different themes. Of course, you can totally run Vampire as a Romantic Comedy if you want, and similarly you can run Scion as a game of humanism, but that wouldn't be entirely true to mythology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T10:24:55-08:00","id":36960,"title":"","content":"I am with Telgar on this, no reservations. I have been in far too many playtests where people derailed\\delayed the project with all these &quot;wouldn't it be cool if we could {thing that had nothing to do with the scope of the game}&quot; add-ons. Not everything needs to be built as a sandbox. Sandboxes can always be added.<br /> <br /> Yes. Yes, it would be cool if you could play as a non-divine character with similar levels of power. I would wholeheartedly back an expansion for that. I do not want the developers to waste cycle time on adding far-from-concept extras if the game is not complete. This Champion\\Immortal\\Godborn idea is the perfect &quot;extra setting&quot; for a new Companion book. If they are putting extra settings in Origins or Hero, put it in there - but not at the expense of the &quot;core&quot; setting.<br /> <br /> I came to this steakhouse for steak. I don't care how perfectly they do sushi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T14:36:14-08:00","id":37019,"title":"","content":"Right; but as I see it, Legendary Beings (Santa Claus, Uncle Sam, etc.) would be \u201csushi\u201d. Champions, Immortals, and Godborn are more like \u201cgrilled vegetables\u201d, \u201csalmon\u201d, and \u201cribs\u201d: they\u2019re the sorts of dishes that you\u2019d expect to find at a steakhouse, to be eaten with or instead of steaks as the customer sees fit. They\u2019re not \u201cextra settings\u201d; they\u2019re the <i>same</i> setting from different, complementary perspectives. And far from detracting from the development of the default setting, they would enrich it: a steakhouse that serves nothing but, say, roast beef would go out of business rather quickly: there would be a few diehards who want just that one dish and nothing else; but most people want more variety than that. <br /> <br /> This isn\u2019t something that has nothing to do with the scope of the game. Most of the ideas I\u2019m presenting here are <i>already in</i> the game; they\u2019re just not presented as playable characters. And the one that technically isn\u2019t in the game fills what I consider to be a gap in the game: the numerous heroes of mythology who were <i>not</i> children of the gods. I keep coming back to Jason because he\u2019s perhaps the most blatant example of a mortal hero who keeps stride with heroic scions; but he is far from the only one. Legendary Mortals don\u2019t cover this, because they\u2019re quickly outclassed by even Heroic scions; and the blood-brothers in <b>Companion</b> (I forget what they\u2019re called) are explicitly in a subservient position relative to Heroic scions, which doesn\u2019t fit the likes of Jason or Odysseus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T15:19:47-08:00","id":37041,"title":"","content":"These things ae in the {rather broken} existing setting. As they were never designed to be playable, they are just as badly designed as every other titanspawn, follower, and whatnot (see the &quot;Amazon as playable character&quot; discussion). There would be considerable cycles taken to redesign and rebalance, especially as OPP* is doing a frame-off restoration of the rules. I do not mind them taking the cycles to do so, but I would rather that they design the game that they are selling (play as half-mortal children of the gods!) before they build a new game in a shared world.<br /> <br /> Nobody complained at the lack of playable Werewolves in the Vampire core book.<br /> <br /> * Yeah, you know me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T15:57:59-08:00","id":37050,"title":"","content":"Immortals probably could use their own book, yes. And I fervently hope that the rebuilding of the setting includes going through the Immortals and Titanspawn and \u201crebalancing\u201d them, for lack of a better term, which would be beneficial in and of itself <i>and</i> would make it easier to include basic Immortals-as-protagonists rules without needing to devote undue word-count to the latter.<br /> <br /> But Champions and Godborn? Those aren\u2019t werewolves in Vampire; they\u2019re more like acolytes and archmasters in Mage, or Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals in Exalted. Heck, <i>immortals</i> aren\u2019t werewolves in Vampire. Will I cry and gnash my teeth if they don\u2019t appear in the core books? No. But I also don\u2019t think they\u2019d be out of place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T17:03:52-08:00","id":37069,"title":"","content":"I would buy the book that they're in. The concept sounds cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1011-phgraves","name":"PHGraves","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1011_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T08:13:10-08:00","id":37331,"title":"","content":"If you ditched the idea of Champions being adopted by Gods, I could probably even get behind them being the same as Heroes. They'd just be capped at Hero forever. It's the fact that they're the same as Scions, except not born special. They earned their special. They're Exalted, in Scion. That bugs the crap outta me. I don't want Scion to become a generic modern fantasy setting, like Exalted turned into a generic anime setting. <br /> <br /> It's pointless to argue about what will and wont be in Scion2, since the writers are still writing and the developers are still developing. They'll decide that. I just hope they don't go for modern fantasy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T08:28:09-08:00","id":37339,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m all for modern fantasy, as long as it isn\u2019t <i>generic</i> modern fantasy and is firmly rooted in authentic mythology. Let the gaming groups build whatever they want on top of that; but keep the foundation grounded in real-world myths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T08:55:26-08:00","id":37357,"title":"","content":"Were I a militant atheist, I would posit that all myths, modern, old, or ancient, are all make-believe.<br /> <br /> That being typed, what makes mythology &quot;authentic?&quot; Were I to create a list of deities, they would look very primal in comparison to what we have had in the past 8k years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T09:09:24-08:00","id":37362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=37357#post37357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Were I a militant atheist, I would posit that all myths, modern, old, or ancient, are all make-believe.<br /> <br /> That being typed, what makes mythology &quot;authentic?&quot; Were I to create a list of deities, they would look very primal in comparison to what we have had in the past 8k years.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need to recognize that structurally there is a difference between myths, legends, and fantasies.<br /> <br /> Myths are traditional stories specifically involving supernatural occurrences or beings. Legends are traditional stories with at least some basis in history/reality from a scholarly perspective.<br /> <br /> Fantasy is a specific fiction genre that borrows from both.<br /> <br /> Mythology's &quot;authenticity&quot; is reliant solely on the traditional nature of the story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T09:37:43-08:00","id":37374,"title":"","content":"That is indeed how I was using the term. As I said, the gaming group is free to build whatever they want \u2014 strike that; they\u2019re <i>encouraged</i> to build whatever they want \u2014 on the foundation that <b>Scion</b> provides. If you wish to introduce an assortment of gods of your own design, or fantastic creatures for your protagonists to face, go for it! But what the core books in <b>Scion</b> should be doing is providing the gods, monsters, and beliefs from long-established real-world mythologies in a form that\u2019s suitable for gaming use. It\u2019s not about what\u2019s make-believe; it\u2019s about what\u2019s traditional: Scion is a game that\u2019s fundamentally rooted in the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T10:28:02-08:00","id":37389,"title":"","content":"Scion itself speaks that language, although from the perspective of atheist it makes a lot of allowances regarding what is a legend. In Scion, the gods and their accomplishments are LEGENDS and not myths. I would hesitate to say that it's a world without myths (because they're all legends, natch) but that's the basic direction you have to be going with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T10:38:49-08:00","id":37394,"title":"","content":"In a world where the supernatural is real, \u201cmyth\u201d and \u201clegend\u201d (per your definitions) aren\u2019t mutually exclusive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T11:07:24-08:00","id":37408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/35860-champions-immortals-and-godborn?p=37394#post37394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a world where the supernatural is real, \u201cmyth\u201d and \u201clegend\u201d (per your definitions) aren\u2019t mutually exclusive.</div> </div> </div> </div>My definitions are textbook, but they are in a few substantial and important cases. Only certain myths are legends in the context of Scion; if all myths were legends we'd have a lot more baggage included in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-26T11:31:42-08:00","id":37417,"title":"","content":"True. My point, though, was that gods being legends does not preclude them from also being myths; <i>not</i> that anything and everything that\u2019s legend and/or myth should be thrown in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}